<BaseLayout title="Cooling System" description="Radiator, fans, IAT placement, heater hoses, and oil cooling for LS Gen Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Cooling System</h1>
  <p>
    LS engines make a lot of heat in a tight bay. Plan radiator capacity, fan strategy, and oil cooling early — especially on BK1 cars with less front clearance.
  </p>

  <h2>Before You Start — Clearance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>BK1:</strong> Prefer Corvette-spacing front accessory drive for maximum room between the engine and radiator fans. F-body (middle) spacing can work but is tighter.</li>
    <li><strong>BK2:</strong> Roughly 1.5" more front clearance than BK1 — more forgiving.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Radiator</h2>
  <p>
    A 3.8 upgraded radiator with a proper fan shroud is strongly recommended.
    Jason Riddle builds these for the community — reach out on Facebook if you need one.
  </p>

  <h2>Fans & Relays</h2>
  <p>Factory radiator fan wires (at the harness):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Red / Orange</strong> — High side (black/red on the fan side)</li>
    <li><strong>Green</strong> — Low side (black/white on the fan side)</li>
    <li><strong>Black</strong> — Ground</li>
  </ul>

  <img src="/images/fan-wiring-bulkhead.jpg" alt="Orange and green factory fan wires at firewall bulkhead" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    Factory fan wires at the bulkhead — orange/red (high) and green (low). Many builders pull these toward the battery for clean relay power.
  </p>

  <p>
    Many builders cut into the harness at the firewall, pull the thick red/green wires toward the battery, and feed new solid-state or conventional relays.
    Holley fan #1 (gray/yellow) and fan #2 (gray/red) typically go to pin 85 as triggered ground on traditional relays.
  </p>

  <img src="/images/fan-controllers-holley.jpg" alt="Holley fan 1 and fan 2 controllers mounted on body" />
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
    Example of Holley fan controllers mounted near the battery.
  </p>

